 "_about": "Annie Fellows Johnston's Little Colonel books, ten of them, dated from each printing's own page: The Little Colonel (1895), The Little Colonel's House Party (this printing 1907), The Little Colonel's Holidays (copyright 1901), The Little Colonel's Hero (copyright 1902), The Little Colonel at Boarding-School (copyright 1903), The Little Colonel in Arizona (copyright 1904), The Little Colonel's Christmas Vacation (copyright 1905), The Little Colonel: Maid of Honor (copyright 1906), The Little Colonel's Knight Comes Riding (copyright 1907) and Mary Ware, the Little Colonel's Chum (copyright 1908; this printing 1944). Her Story of the Red Cross is not taken. The books are set in the post-war South and their Black characters speak and are drawn in the terms of their time. Added at the coordinator's standing relay (2026-10-02/03: choose public-domain storytellers batches; Adam may veto).",
